      <div type="clause" n="53.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 53.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> wite, hwa ðæs deadan ierfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.24"/> hæbbe, tieme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.16"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> to þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24a" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.24a"/> ierfe ⁊ bidde ða hond þe þæt ierfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.24"/> hafað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gedó þone ceap<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.25"/> unbeceasne oþþe gecyðe, þæt se deada<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.26"/> næfre þæt ierfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.24"/> ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.5"/> wite, hwá ðæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.20-2"/> deadan yrfe hæbbe, tyme ðonne to þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> yrfe ⁊ bidde ða hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.5"/> þe þæt yrfe hafeþ, ðæt he him gedó ðone ceap unbesacene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.21-2"/> oþþe gecyþe, ðæt se deada næfre þæt yrfe ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he ðonne wite, hwá ðæs deadan yrfe hæbbe, tyme ðonne to ðam yrfe ⁊ bidde ða hónd þe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> yrfe hafað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he him gedó ðone ceap unbesacene oððe gecyðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se deade næfre þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> yrfe ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="113" ed="#liebermann"/>Si tunc sciat, quis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.17"/> mortui pecuniam hereditauit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.18"/>, appellet in ipsam pecuniam et roget ipsam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.19"/> manum, ut hoc captale quietum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.20"/> ei faciat uel ostendat, quod nunquam ipsius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.21"/> mortui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.22"/> pecunia fuerit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.23"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="54" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he þonne wite, hwa ðæs deadan ierfe hæbbe, tieme þonne to þam ierfe<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Ine_53-1.attnote.fn.8"/> ⁊ bidde ða hond þe þæt ierfe hafað, þæt he him gedó þone ceap unbeceasne<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_53-1.attnote.fn.9"/> oþþe gecyðe, þæt se deada<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_53-1.attnote.fn.10"/> næfre þæt ierfe ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="56.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="416" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif he þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> wite hwa ðæs deadan ierfe hæbbe, tieme þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> to þam ierfe ⁊ bidde ða hond þe þæt ierfe hafað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gedó þone ceap unbeceasne oþþe gecyðe, þæt se deada næfre þæt ierfe ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="113" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er jedoch weiss, wer des Todten Erbnachlass besitzt, dann ziehe er [die Gewähr] auf diesen Erbnachlass und fordere die Hand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.de.1"/>, die den Erbnachlass besitzt, auf, dass er [der Erbe] ihm [entweder] den Kaufgegenstand unbestritten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.de.2"/> mache<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.de.3"/> oder beweise, dass jener Todte niemals diese<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_53-1.lnote.de.4"/> Fahrhabe besessen habe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he knows who possesses the dead man’s estate, then let him vouch [to warranty] upon that estate and call upon the hand that possesses the estate, that he [the heir] either make the purchased item undisputed for him or prove that the dead man never possessed that property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="55" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, he knows who has succeeded to the estate<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_53-1.attnote.n.1"/> of the dead man, he shall vouch the estate to warranty, and demand of the man who holds the estate that he shall make [his title to] the chattel<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_53-1.attnote.n.2"/> incontestable, or declare that the dead man never owned the property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="406" ed="#whitelock"/>If, however, he knows who has the dead man’s inheritance, he is then to vouch the inheritance to warranty, and ask the person that has the inheritance to make that purchase<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_53-1.whinote.n.1"/> incontestable, or to declare that the dead man never owned that property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="417" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If he, however, knows who owns the dead man’s inheritance, let him then vouch the estate to warranty and request of the man [<hi rend="italic">hand</hi>] that has the inheritance, that he grant him the property uncontested or declare that the dead man never owned [that property as part of] the inheritance.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quod <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quod Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dauit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dauit K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eum <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> i. m. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eum instead of i. m. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei q. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei q. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">m. i. <hi rend="italic">KCo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">m. i. KCo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fuit <hi rend="italic">LondMHkT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fuit LondMHkT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53-1.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
